# =====================================================================
# KanjiMon — Environment Variables Template
# =====================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your real values.
# `.env.local` is gitignored. NEVER commit real secrets.
#
# Generate a fresh key here: https://supabase.com/dashboard → Settings
#   → API → Project API keys → "anon public" (NOT service_role)
# =====================================================================

# --- Supabase (Cloud sync + auth + leaderboard) -----------------------
# Get these from: https://supabase.com/dashboard → Project → Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...PASTE_YOUR_ANON_KEY_HERE

# Optional: URL to redirect to after email confirmation / OAuth
# (defaults to the origin if not set)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3210

# =====================================================================
# How to enable live features:
# =====================================================================
# 1. Sign up / sign in to https://supabase.com (free tier is fine)
# 2. Create a new project (wait ~2 min for provisioning)
# 3. Project Settings → API → copy URL + anon public key into this file
# 4. Save as `.env.local` (no leading dot in the filename when copying)
# 5. Restart `npm run dev` (Next.js loads env on start)
# 6. Run the SQL migration:
#      - Open https://supabase.com/dashboard → SQL Editor → New query
#      - Paste contents of supabase/migrations/0001_leaderboard_scores.sql
#      - Click "Run"
# 7. Visit http://localhost:3210/leaderboard — you should see
#    "Mode global" instead of "Mode lokal"
#
# Verification: `node scripts/check-supabase.mjs` (must print "OK")
#
# To DISABLE cloud features: delete or comment out both lines above.
# The app will gracefully fall back to local-only mode.
